WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.069
Shapes are all around you.
Some are flat. Some are solid.

2
00:00:08.289 --> 00:00:12.422
You can also compare their sizes.
Longer, heavier, holds more.

3
00:00:12.922 --> 00:00:16.684
A flat shape lies on the page.
You could draw it yourself.

4
00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:21.037
Here is a square. Count its
sides: one, two, three, four.

5
00:00:21.257 --> 00:00:24.833
Four sides. Now the corners,
where two sides meet.

6
00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:28.861
One, two, three, four. A
square has four corners too.

7
00:00:29.081 --> 00:00:32.146
A triangle has three
sides and three corners.

8
00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:37.195
A circle is different. Its edge
curves right round, with no corners.

9
00:00:37.695 --> 00:00:41.503
A solid shape is not flat.
You can hold it in your hand.

10
00:00:41.723 --> 00:00:45.671
A cube is like a dice. Its
flat surfaces are called faces.

11
00:00:45.891 --> 00:00:49.188
Count them: one, two, three,
four, five, six faces.

12
00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:53.541
An edge is where two faces
meet. A cube has twelve edges.

13
00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:57.476
A sphere is like a ball.
One curved face, no edges.

14
00:00:57.696 --> 00:01:01.597
A cylinder is like a tin.
A cone has a point on top.

15
00:01:02.097 --> 00:01:04.791
How do you tell a flat
shape from a solid one?

16
00:01:05.011 --> 00:01:08.447
Ask one question. Could I
pick it up and turn it over?

17
00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:13.311
A circle is drawn on paper, so
it is flat. A ball you can hold.

18
00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:17.850
A square is flat. A cube is
solid, made of six square faces.

19
00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.462
Here are three ribbons,
all of different lengths.

20
00:01:21.682 --> 00:01:24.282
Line up one end, so
they all start together.

21
00:01:24.502 --> 00:01:27.753
Now see which one goes
further. This one is short.

22
00:01:27.973 --> 00:01:31.271
This one is longer. And this
one is the longest of all.

23
00:01:31.771 --> 00:01:34.557
Which one is heavier?
A balance can tell you.

24
00:01:34.777 --> 00:01:38.167
Put a melon in one pan and
a strawberry in the other.

25
00:01:38.387 --> 00:01:41.220
The side that goes down
holds the heavier thing.

26
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.387
The melon side goes down.
So the melon is heavier.

27
00:01:45.887 --> 00:01:48.859
Capacity means how much
a container can hold.

28
00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:52.562
This jug is full. The water
is right up to the top.

29
00:01:52.782 --> 00:01:55.615
This one is empty. It has none at all.

30
00:01:55.835 --> 00:01:59.225
In between, the jug where the
water is higher holds more.

31
00:01:59.725 --> 00:02:04.973
Flat shapes have sides and corners.
Solid shapes have faces and edges.

32
00:02:05.193 --> 00:02:08.444
A flat shape you draw. A
solid shape you can hold.

33
00:02:08.664 --> 00:02:13.122
Longer, heavier, holds more:
you can compare any two things.

34
00:02:13.342 --> 00:02:15.478
Now go and hunt for shapes at home.
